1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,410
Lightning hits a field.

2
00:00:01,410 --> 00:00:02,760
The flash disappears.

3
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:04,360
A cow is standing nearby.

4
00:00:04,450 --> 00:00:06,470
A car is parked beside the road.

5
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:08,000
And beneath the grass,

6
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,840
something is happening you can't see.

7
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:11,800
Where did all that electricity go?

8
00:00:12,578 --> 00:00:13,488
I hit the ground.

9
00:00:13,488 --> 00:00:14,165
Job done?

10
00:00:14,795 --> 00:00:16,395
The ground isn't a trash can.

11
00:00:17,012 --> 00:00:18,062
During the strike,

12
00:00:18,062 --> 00:00:20,524
current spreads through and along the ground.

13
00:00:20,844 --> 00:00:21,384
First,

14
00:00:21,384 --> 00:00:24,574
the bright line is glowing air along a conducting channel.

15
00:00:24,864 --> 00:00:27,834
It isn't a solid yellow object diving into a hole.

16
00:00:28,094 --> 00:00:29,434
Electric charge moves;

17
00:00:29,454 --> 00:00:32,794
the cartoon bolt is just our very confident tour guide.

18
00:00:33,264 --> 00:00:33,664
Wait.

19
00:00:33,664 --> 00:00:34,984
I don't live underground now?

20
00:00:35,482 --> 00:00:35,862
Thankfully,

21
00:00:35,862 --> 00:00:36,307
no.

22
00:00:36,627 --> 00:00:38,987
A strike involves brief pulses of current.

23
00:00:39,157 --> 00:00:41,397
A flash may contain several strokes.

24
00:00:41,617 --> 00:00:44,157
We're slowing one moment down to see the paths.

25
00:00:44,567 --> 00:00:44,857
This is

26
00:00:44,857 --> 00:00:48,337
not electricity flowing underground for the next five minutes.

27
00:00:49,997 --> 00:00:51,687
Imagine a network of routes,

28
00:00:51,687 --> 00:00:53,937
not one tunnel to the center of the Earth.

29
00:00:54,267 --> 00:00:56,697
Current can divide among available paths.

30
00:00:57,287 --> 00:01:00,207
How it spreads depends on the electrical properties of the

31
00:01:00,207 --> 00:01:00,857
ground

32
00:01:00,857 --> 00:01:02,427
and the things connected to it.

33
00:01:03,554 --> 00:01:06,254
So there's no express elevator to the Earth's core?

34
00:01:06,812 --> 00:01:07,732
I have layers.

35
00:01:07,732 --> 00:01:08,737
Not a front desk.

36
00:01:09,357 --> 00:01:10,807
Soil isn't all the same.

37
00:01:10,867 --> 00:01:13,787
Water carrying dissolved ions can make some ground more

38
00:01:13,787 --> 00:01:14,647
conductive.

39
00:01:15,047 --> 00:01:16,127
Dry patches,

40
00:01:16,137 --> 00:01:17,127
different minerals,

41
00:01:17,127 --> 00:01:20,187
layers and buried conductors can change the routes.

42
00:01:20,307 --> 00:01:23,407
A tidy circle on a diagram is only a simplification.

43
00:01:23,964 --> 00:01:25,574
The charge is redistributed;

44
00:01:25,924 --> 00:01:27,914
it doesn't turn into heat and vanish.

45
00:01:28,234 --> 00:01:31,174
Electrical energy is transferred into other forms,

46
00:01:31,284 --> 00:01:32,294
including heat.

47
00:01:32,474 --> 00:01:35,564
That distinction explains one of the strangest souvenirs a

48
00:01:35,564 --> 00:01:37,404
lightning strike can leave behind.

49
00:01:38,447 --> 00:01:39,287
And now the sand is...

50
00:01:39,287 --> 00:01:39,917
glass?

51
00:01:40,664 --> 00:01:42,126
I requested a beach day.

52
00:01:42,553 --> 00:01:43,843
Under suitable conditions,

53
00:01:43,843 --> 00:01:46,813
lightning can heat silica-rich sand enough to fuse it into

54
00:01:46,813 --> 00:01:49,043
glassy structures called fulgurites.

55
00:01:49,363 --> 00:01:50,663
Some form irregular,

56
00:01:50,663 --> 00:01:53,453
branching tubes around the path of the discharge.

57
00:01:53,873 --> 00:01:56,493
Nature has effectively drawn in glass.

58
00:01:57,386 --> 00:01:59,126
But not every strike makes one.

59
00:01:59,576 --> 00:02:01,426
The material and conditions matter.

60
00:02:02,036 --> 00:02:04,946
A fulgurite is evidence of an intense heating event,

61
00:02:04,946 --> 00:02:06,706
not a jar of trapped electricity.

62
00:02:07,196 --> 00:02:08,046
Once cooled,

63
00:02:08,066 --> 00:02:10,498
it can remain long after the flash is gone.

64
00:02:11,468 --> 00:02:11,948
New look.

65
00:02:11,948 --> 00:02:13,106
Extremely fragile.

66
00:02:13,426 --> 00:02:15,796
That glassy souvenir is the aftermath.

67
00:02:15,796 --> 00:02:18,386
Now rewind to the strike itself.

68
00:02:18,606 --> 00:02:21,576
The immediate danger isn't finding an interesting rock.

69
00:02:21,846 --> 00:02:23,866
It's becoming part of a conducting route

70
00:02:23,936 --> 00:02:25,146
while the pulse is happening.

71
00:02:25,996 --> 00:02:27,476
So where you stand matters?

72
00:02:28,003 --> 00:02:29,493
And where both feet stand.

73
00:02:29,923 --> 00:02:32,733
Your feet can touch places at different voltages.

74
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:35,573
That difference can drive current through your body.

75
00:02:36,518 --> 00:02:38,698
Think of voltage as an electrical level.

76
00:02:38,878 --> 00:02:41,448
Two contact points can be at different levels,

77
00:02:41,448 --> 00:02:43,368
even on the same patch of ground.

78
00:02:43,698 --> 00:02:45,458
The difference between them matters.

79
00:02:45,708 --> 00:02:49,158
The body can provide another route connecting those points.

80
00:02:50,263 --> 00:02:52,293
This is often called step voltage.

81
00:02:52,643 --> 00:02:54,873
The actual difference depends on the strike,

82
00:02:54,923 --> 00:02:57,103
ground and contact positions.

83
00:02:57,383 --> 00:02:59,663
It is not identical for every stance,

84
00:02:59,953 --> 00:03:02,843
and this diagram cannot tell you a safe distance to stand

85
00:03:02,843 --> 00:03:03,513
outside.

86
00:03:04,483 --> 00:03:05,583
I have four feet.

87
00:03:05,663 --> 00:03:06,658
Is that a problem?

88
00:03:07,356 --> 00:03:09,996
A cow's front and back feet can be farther apart

89
00:03:09,996 --> 00:03:11,376
than a person's feet.

90
00:03:11,976 --> 00:03:14,356
That can span a larger voltage difference.

91
00:03:15,286 --> 00:03:18,336
Ground current is one reason lightning can injure animals

92
00:03:18,336 --> 00:03:19,806
that were not struck directly.

93
00:03:20,126 --> 00:03:22,326
I'd like to unsubscribe from outside.

94
00:03:22,646 --> 00:03:24,696
Ground current isn't the only hazard.

95
00:03:25,146 --> 00:03:26,196
A direct strike,

96
00:03:26,196 --> 00:03:28,056
contact with conducting objects

97
00:03:28,056 --> 00:03:31,156
and a side flash from a nearby object are other ways

98
00:03:31,156 --> 00:03:32,596
lightning can affect someone.

99
00:03:32,976 --> 00:03:35,866
Missing the visible bolt does not settle the question.

100
00:03:36,816 --> 00:03:38,204
That escalated quickly.

101
00:03:38,524 --> 00:03:41,834
So why might someone inside a car be better protected?

102
00:03:42,224 --> 00:03:45,184
The answer is not the one part of the car touching the road.

103
00:03:46,315 --> 00:03:48,175
My tires are taking all the credit.

104
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:49,790
In an enclosed,

105
00:03:49,790 --> 00:03:51,540
hard-topped metal vehicle,

106
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:54,440
the conducting body can provide a route around the occupied

107
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:55,160
space.

108
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:57,270
Current can travel along the outside

109
00:03:57,270 --> 00:03:58,980
and onward toward the ground.

110
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:01,670
The protective idea is the shell,

111
00:04:01,670 --> 00:04:03,572
not a magical rubber barrier.

112
00:04:04,542 --> 00:04:06,382
So the tires aren't the superhero?

113
00:04:06,762 --> 00:04:08,082
Have you seen the rest of me?

114
00:04:09,307 --> 00:04:11,987
Lightning has already crossed a huge gap through air.

115
00:04:12,277 --> 00:04:15,787
A tire is not the reason the vehicle can protect its occupants.

116
00:04:16,407 --> 00:04:20,420
Lightning can also damage tires and other parts of a vehicle.

117
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:22,330
The kind of vehicle matters.

118
00:04:22,730 --> 00:04:25,440
A closed hard-topped metal vehicle is different from a

119
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:27,290
convertible or an open cart.

120
00:04:27,690 --> 00:04:28,950
Keep the windows closed

121
00:04:28,950 --> 00:04:30,970
and avoid touching conducting parts.

122
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:33,440
This is protection under conditions,

123
00:04:33,730 --> 00:04:35,660
not a promise of invincibility.

124
00:04:36,172 --> 00:04:38,122
Please stop testing this outside.

125
00:04:38,442 --> 00:04:40,252
And what tells you to stop the picnic

126
00:04:40,252 --> 00:04:42,222
before you see a nearby strike?

127
00:04:42,692 --> 00:04:43,392
Thunder.

128
00:04:43,912 --> 00:04:46,612
Lightning rapidly heats the air along its channel.

129
00:04:46,702 --> 00:04:48,352
The air expands suddenly,

130
00:04:48,432 --> 00:04:51,305
creating the pressure disturbance we hear as thunder.

131
00:04:51,625 --> 00:04:53,765
The noise is the air throwing a tantrum?

132
00:04:54,498 --> 00:04:55,908
An energetic way to put it.

133
00:04:56,638 --> 00:04:59,838
Thunder means lightning is close enough to take seriously.

134
00:05:00,278 --> 00:05:02,108
Don't wait for the rain to reach you,

135
00:05:02,108 --> 00:05:04,578
or for a flash to look impressively close.

136
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:05,920
Hear thunder?

137
00:05:05,950 --> 00:05:07,710
Get inside a substantial building.

138
00:05:08,388 --> 00:05:11,028
An enclosed building is a much better place to shelter

139
00:05:11,028 --> 00:05:12,258
than an open field.

140
00:05:12,808 --> 00:05:13,588
Once inside,

141
00:05:13,588 --> 00:05:15,048
stay away from windows,

142
00:05:15,098 --> 00:05:18,098
plumbing and corded electrical equipment during the storm.

143
00:05:18,568 --> 00:05:20,725
Indoor precautions still matter.

144
00:05:21,045 --> 00:05:22,605
Wait at least thirty minutes

145
00:05:22,605 --> 00:05:25,375
after the last thunder before going back outside.

146
00:05:26,175 --> 00:05:29,195
Rain easing is not the same as the lightning risk ending.

147
00:05:29,725 --> 00:05:32,515
The storm doesn't have to be directly overhead to matter.

148
00:05:33,378 --> 00:05:34,158
A tree,

149
00:05:34,158 --> 00:05:36,408
an open-sided shelter or a fence is

150
00:05:36,408 --> 00:05:38,528
not a substitute for proper shelter.

151
00:05:38,838 --> 00:05:41,768
Nor is there a special patch of outdoor ground this little

152
00:05:41,768 --> 00:05:43,828
cartoon can certify as safe.

153
00:05:44,248 --> 00:05:44,518
So...

154
00:05:44,518 --> 00:05:45,808
where am I supposed to go?

155
00:05:46,793 --> 00:05:47,806
That's your problem.

156
00:05:48,126 --> 00:05:49,650
Yours is finding shelter.
